Appendix J: Numerical Simulation Framework

J.1 Governing Equations

The system is described by the coupled ODEs:

\frac{dC_w}{dt} = \frac{R_{\text{detach}} - \lambda C_w}{V}

\frac{dC_{\text{text}}}{dt} = -k_{\text{detach}} C_{\text{text}} + k_{\text{redep}} C_w

\frac{dT}{dt} = \frac{P_{\text{heater}} - h A (T - T_\infty)}{m c_p}

\frac{d\text{MPF}}{dt} = K \tau^a T^b

J.2 Discretization

Using explicit Euler with time step  \Delta t :

C_w^{n+1} = C_w^n + \Delta t \frac{R_{\text{detach}}^n - \lambda C_w^n}{V}

C_{\text{text}}^{n+1} = C_{\text{text}}^n + \Delta t \left(-k_{\text{detach}} C_{\text{text}}^n + k_{\text{redep}} C_w^n\right)

T^{n+1} = T^n + \Delta t \frac{P_{\text{heater}} - h A (T^n - T_\infty)}{m c_p}

\text{MPF}^{n+1} = \text{MPF}^n + \Delta t K (\tau^n)^a (T^n)^b

J.3 Stability Criterion

For explicit Euler, the time step must satisfy:

\Delta t < \frac{2}{\lambda / V}

For  \lambda / V \sim 0.1  s⁻¹,  \Delta t < 20  s. A time step of 1 s is conservative and stable.

