Appendix L: Proof of Convergence for Adaptive Stop

L.1 Statement

Theorem. Under the adaptive stop criterion:

t_{\text{stop}} = \inf\left\{ t : \left| \frac{dC_w}{dt} \right| < \epsilon \ \text{and} \ C_w < C_{\text{threshold}} \right\}

the cycle terminates in finite time with probability 1.

L.2 Proof

From the closed-loop mass balance:

\frac{dC_w}{dt} = \frac{R_{\text{detach}} - \lambda C_w}{V}

As  t \to \infty ,  C_w \to C_w(\infty) = R_{\text{detach}} / \lambda . Therefore:

\frac{dC_w}{dt} \to 0

For any  \epsilon > 0 , there exists  t_\epsilon  such that  |dC_w/dt| < \epsilon  for all  t > t_\epsilon . If  C_w(\infty) < C_{\text{threshold}} , then  C_w(t) < C_{\text{threshold}}  for sufficiently large  t . The stop condition is satisfied in finite time. \square

L.3 Corollary

If  C_w(\infty) > C_{\text{threshold}} , the cycle does not terminate under the adaptive criterion, and a fault condition is indicated. The controller must either increase the capture rate, increase the detachment rate, or abort the cycle.

