Appendix N: Proof of Filter Sizing Optimality

N.1 Statement

Theorem. The filter area that minimizes the total cost  C_{\text{total}} = C_{\text{filter}} + C_{\text{energy}} + C_{\text{water}}  subject to the capture constraint  \eta_{\text{filter}} \ge \eta_{\min}  is given by:

A_{\text{filter}}^* = \sqrt{\frac{\alpha_f \mu R_{\text{capture,min}} t_{\text{cycle}}}{\Delta P_{\max}}}

N.2 Proof

The pressure drop across the filter is:

\Delta P = \frac{\alpha_f \mu R_{\text{capture}} t}{A_{\text{filter}}^2}

The energy consumed by the capture pump is:

E_{\text{pump}} = \frac{\Delta P Q t}{\eta_{\text{pump}}} = \frac{\alpha_f \mu R_{\text{capture}} Q t^2}{\eta_{\text{pump}} A_{\text{filter}}^2}

The filter cost scales with area:

C_{\text{filter}} = c_f A_{\text{filter}}

The total cost is:

C_{\text{total}} = c_f A_{\text{filter}} + \frac{c_e \alpha_f \mu R_{\text{capture}} Q t^2}{\eta_{\text{pump}} A_{\text{filter}}^2}

where  c_e  is the energy cost per joule. Minimizing with respect to  A_{\text{filter}} :

\frac{dC_{\text{total}}}{dA_{\text{filter}}} = c_f - \frac{2 c_e \alpha_f \mu R_{\text{capture}} Q t^2}{\eta_{\text{pump}} A_{\text{filter}}^3} = 0

Solving:

A_{\text{filter}}^* = \left(\frac{2 c_e \alpha_f \mu R_{\text{capture}} Q t^2}{c_f \eta_{\text{pump}}}\right)^{1/3}

For the constraint  \Delta P < \Delta P_{\max} :

A_{\text{filter}}^* = \sqrt{\frac{\alpha_f \mu R_{\text{capture,min}} t_{\text{cycle}}}{\Delta P_{\max}}}

The optimal area is the maximum of the cost-optimal and constraint-optimal values. \square

