Appendix U: Proof of Sensor Fusion Improvement

U.1 Statement

Theorem. The Kalman filter estimate  \hat{x}  has lower variance than any single-sensor estimate.

U.2 Proof

The Kalman filter combines the prior estimate  \hat{x}^-  with variance  P^-  and the measurement  y  with variance  R . The posterior variance is:

P = \left( (P^-)^{-1} + H^T R^{-1} H \right)^{-1}

For scalar  x  and  H = 1 :

P = \frac{1}{1/P^- + 1/R}

Since  1/P^- + 1/R > 1/P^-  and  > 1/R , we have  P < P^-  and  P < R . The fused estimate has lower variance than either the prior or the measurement alone. \square

U.3 Multi-Sensor Fusion

For  n  sensors with variances  R_1, \ldots, R_n :

P = \left( \frac{1}{P^-} + \sum_{i=1}^n \frac{1}{R_i} \right)^{-1}

The variance decreases monotonically with each additional sensor. The marginal benefit of each sensor diminishes as  1/R_i  decreases.

