    PARETO DOMINANCE PROOF:
    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │                                                                             │
    │   Definition: x* is Pareto optimal if no feasible x exists such that:       │
    │                                                                             │
    │   J_i(x) ≤ J_i(x*) for all i, with strict inequality for at least one i     │
    │                                                                             │
    │   Theorem: If ATDS achieves J_E < J_E,conv AND J_MPF < J_MPF,conv,         │
    │            then ATDS is Pareto-dominant over conventional.                  │
    │                                                                             │
    │   Proof:                                                                    │
    │   Let x_conv be a conventional design point with objectives:                │
    │   J(x_conv) = [J_E,conv, J_MPF,conv]                                       │
    │                                                                             │
    │   Let x_ATDS be an ATDS design point with objectives:                       │
    │   J(x_ATDS) = [J_E,ATDS, J_MPF,ATDS]                                       │
    │                                                                             │
    │   If J_E,ATDS < J_E,conv and J_MPF,ATDS < J_MPF,conv,                       │
    │   then J_i(x_ATDS) < J_i(x_conv) for all i (both components)               │
    │                                                                             │
    │   Therefore x_conv is Pareto-dominated by x_ATDS.                          │
    │   Therefore ATDS is Pareto-dominant.                                        │
    │                                                                             │
    │   QED                                                                       │
    │                                                                             │
